    {version:'v3.3.0',date:'1 November 2026',sections:[{title:'Added',items:['<strong>LearnCraft : Master Canvas Extractor</strong> reads the structure and timing of an open LearnCraft course, including its parts, sections, missions, subsections and assets, and comes with several useful features.','<strong>LearnCraft : Ultimate Go Live</strong> helps take a Master Canvas and its linked variants to Ready from the web app or extension popup.']},{title:'Changed',items:['The landing page now groups tools into SMART Notebook, Image Tools and LearnCraft categories.','Loy Krathong festival!']},{title:'Fixed',items:['<strong>SMART Notebook : Convert to PDF</strong> keeps pages that cannot be drawn in their original position as crossed-out blank pages, so later PDF pages stay in the correct order.']}]},
    {version:'v3.2.1',date:'29 October 2026',sections:[{title:'Added',items:['Hover over a Quick Guide step to highlight the related controls in its tool.','After choosing a tool, press Space to switch to the next tool. The shortcut is shown in the tool selector.','New home screen animation.','A small redesign of the About Us page.']}]},
    {version:'v3.2.0',date:'28 October 2026',sections:[{title:'Added',items:['New home screen with a card for each tool. Press Space to jump straight into <strong>File creator</strong>.','Tools now live in a side list grouped by category. Press 1–4 to switch tools. This replaces the old carousel and the All Tools window.','Each tool has a Quick Guide with short steps and a Detailed Guide &amp; Tips section. Press I to open or close the detailed guide.','<strong>File creator</strong>: Up / Down arrow keys now move the selection in the image list.','The About Us page now shows the project line count.','A warning appears if you try to close the tab while a tool is working, or while <strong>File creator</strong> still holds images.']},{title:'Changed',items:['<strong>Convert to pdf</strong> always keeps the original page size, so the Sharpness option is gone. Only JPEG quality remains (default 90%).','<strong>Image Resizer</strong> now defaults to 100% JPEG / WebP quality (was 75%).','<strong>Convert to pdf</strong> skips videos, audio and thumbnails inside notebooks, so big files convert faster and use less memory.','<strong>File creator</strong> is smoother: clicking a row no longer rebuilds the whole list, and the same preview is not decoded twice.','Tool layouts now adapt better to narrow screens. On wider screens, the tool selector stays on the left and Quick Guide stays on the right, with both panels at equal height.','<strong>Image Resizer</strong>: Reset to defaults now aligns with JPEG / WebP quality, the output-folder control has moved up, and the dropzone fills the available space.','Long jobs no longer slow down when the browser tab is in the background.','<strong>Page locker</strong> asks for save permission for each file picked one by one, and falls back to download if refused.','Cleaner buttons and a tidier Release Notes timeline line.']},{title:'Fixed',items:['Notebooks with <strong>Thai file names</strong>: images were silently dropped in <strong>Convert to pdf</strong> and could break in <strong>Page locker</strong>. Names are now read correctly, and Thai names are kept when the file is saved back.','<strong>Image Resizer</strong> never overwrites the original when a file with the same name exists.','<strong>Convert to pdf</strong> no longer shows one browser permission prompt per .notebook file.']}]},
    {version:'v3.1.5',date:'27 October 2026',sections:[{title:'Changed',items:['<strong>SMART Notebook : Convert to pdf</strong> now converts with a built-in converter that runs in your browser instead of downloading a PDF engine of about 30 MB. The tool is ready instantly, the setup steps are gone, and it uses less memory.','Very large pages are now scaled down to fit the limit of the browser, which is needed on iPhone and iPad. A page that takes longer than 60 seconds to draw is skipped and reported instead of freezing the conversion.','Removed the old PDF engine files that earlier versions stored in your browser, freeing about 30 MB.']}]},
    {version:'v3.1.4',date:'26 October 2026',sections:[{title:'Fixed',items:['Fixed the cursor glow in <strong>SMART Notebook : File creator</strong> covering the image preview, disappearing from the file list after adding files, and staying frozen after dragging files in.','Fixed <strong>SMART Notebook : Convert to pdf</strong> showing "PDF tools ready." and a full progress bar before setup had actually finished.']},{title:'Changed',items:['<strong>SMART Notebook : Convert to pdf</strong> now shows how many setup steps are done and how many are left before the PDF tools are ready.']}]},
    {version:'v3.1.3',date:'22 October 2026',sections:[{title:'Fixed',items:['Fixed the <strong>Image Resizer</strong> error message so it lists the files that could not be processed.','Fixed <strong>Image Resizer</strong> retrying files that are too large or damaged on the main page, which could freeze the browser. Very large images are now refused with a clear message instead of crashing the tab, and the time allowed per image grows with its size.','Fixed new updates sometimes not loading because of stale cached files, including old PDF engine files staying in the browser after an engine update and a failed engine start never being retried.','Fixed <strong>SMART Notebook : Convert to pdf</strong> logic by adding the fast path. Pages with no handwriting are now processed faster.','Fixed <strong>Convert to pdf</strong> losing finished PDFs when the browser would not let it save into the folder: they are downloaded instead.','Fixed <strong>SMART Notebook : File creator</strong> moving a row to the end when it was dropped outside the list, and rows sometimes refusing to drag.']},{title:'Added',items:['An <strong>Original size</strong> option in <strong>SMART Notebook : Convert to PDF</strong> prevents pictures from being shrunk.','<strong>SMART Notebook : Convert to PDF</strong> now includes an <strong>Overwrite all</strong> option.','<strong>Image Resizer</strong> now offers JPEG / WebP quality controls, warns when images are stretched, and notes when WebP cannot store DPI.']},{title:'Changed',items:['Improved <strong>Image Resizer</strong> performance by reducing memory use by about half, and results are now saved as soon as each file finishes. (processes 30% faster)','Images that already have the requested size now only get their DPI changed, with no re-compression.','<strong>Image Resizer</strong> results are now downloaded as one zip file when the browser cannot save into a folder.','Pictures are decoded once instead of twice in <strong>SMART Notebook : File creator</strong>, so notebooks are built faster.']}]},
    {version:'v3.1.2',date:'20 October 2026',sections:[{title:'Changed',items:['Improved <strong>Image Resizer</strong> performance with parallel file processing, making it 6x faster than before.']}]},
    {version:'v3.1.1',date:'20 October 2026',sections:[{title:'Added',items:['The fullscreen preview in <strong>SMART Notebook : File Creator</strong> now has zoom controls; use the mouse wheel or the buttons on the right.','You can drag to pan the fullscreen preview in <strong>SMART Notebook : File Creator</strong> while zoomed in.']},{title:'Changed',items:['The fullscreen preview now opens at the zoom level you were viewing in the preview pane.']},{title:'Fixed',items:['Fixed the fullscreen preview button in <strong>SMART Notebook : File creator</strong> not responding while the image was zoomed in.']}]},
    {version:'v3.1.0',date:'19 October 2026',sections:[{title:'Added',items:['The preview in <strong>SMART Notebook : File Creator</strong> can now be panned while zoomed in.','Alt + click opens an image at full size in <strong>SMART Notebook : File Creator</strong>.','The Release Notes page now includes animations.','Press Space to start the recommended tool.']},{title:'Changed',items:['Prevented the A/D keys from switching tools while a popup is open.','Improved <strong>SMART Notebook : File creator</strong> and <strong>SMART Notebook : Page locker</strong> performance.']}]},
    {version:'v3.0.0',date:'16 October 2026',transition:true,sections:[{title:'Changed',items:['Moved from the Windows .exe application to a web app, with a redesigned interface and tools that run in your browser.']}]},
    {version:'v2.2.1',date:'13 October 2026',sections:[{title:'Added',items:['<strong>SMART Notebook : File Creator</strong> now shows a translucent preview of an image while you drag it.']},{title:'Changed',items:['Improved the display while dragging image files in <strong>SMART Notebook : File creator</strong>.','Improved the feel of dragging image files in <strong>SMART Notebook : File creator</strong>.']},{title:'Fixed',items:['Fixed each tool window so it returns to its default size when switching tools.']}]},
    {version:'v2.2.0',date:'12 October 2026',sections:[{title:'Important',items:['Updates from older versions may take slightly longer. Please do not close the app until the update finishes (within 2 minutes).']},{title:'Changed',items:['Reworked the app to use hidden-portable logic for faster startup.']},{title:'Fixed',items:['Improved icon sharpness.']}]},
    {version:'v2.1.1',date:'3 October 2026',sections:[{title:'Changed',items:['Renamed <strong>SMART Notebook : Convert to pdf</strong>.','Updated instructions for <strong>SMART Notebook : File creator</strong> and <strong>Image Resizer</strong>.']},{title:'Fixed',items:['Adjusted the <strong>Image Resizer</strong> drop zone.']}]},
    {version:'v2.1.0',date:'30 September 2026',sections:[{title:'Added',items:['<strong>SMART Notebook : Convert to PDF</strong> is now available.']},{title:'Changed',items:['Changed library handling to reduce app size.']}]},
    {version:'v2.0.0',date:'24 September 2026',sections:[{title:'Added',items:['<strong>SMART Notebook : File Creator</strong> creates SMART Notebook files from images.']},{title:'Changed',items:['Renamed <strong>PageLock</strong> to <strong>SMART Notebook : Page locker</strong>.','Improved startup and changed tool selection to a dropdown.','Updated the title bar and pop-up theme.','Updated tool instructions.']},{title:'Fixed',items:['Fixed pop-up positioning.','Fixed background logic for each tool.']}]},
    {version:'v1.0.1',date:'22 September 2026',sections:[{title:'Changed',items:['Updated the instructions on the About Us page.']}]},{version:'v1.0.0',date:'22 September 2026',sections:[{title:'Release',items:['First release of .exe format.']}]},
    {version:'v0.0.0',date:'June 2024',sections:[{paragraphs:[
      `I started this project because creating course materials in SMART Notebook felt repetitive and time-consuming. It was even more work for LearnCraft courses, where each question has its own page.`,
      `Locking every page meant clicking through the file and locking each one by hand. I thought a program could automate that. But .notebook is a fairly specialized file format, and there weren’t many tools online for working with it. It’s an older format developed by an EdTech company (or so I believe), so I decided to build a tool on my own.`,
      `The first version could do just one thing: lock every page in a .notebook file. It worked by using graphical user interface (GUI) automation to simulate mouse clicks and keyboard presses, going through the pages one by one. It turned out that performance varied from device to device. The process depended on the system’s speed, so it could be unreliable on slower ones.`,
      `It was the first solution that came to my mind. I was tired of clicking and locking every page myself, so I wrote a program to do the clicking for me. Simple enough, right? lol`,
      `Since it didn’t work reliably on every device, I went back and investigated the .notebook file structure. After a lot of research, I found that it’s a type of ZIP archive containing several kinds of data. (You can even try it yourself: change a .notebook file’s extension to .zip and open it.) The pages are stored as .svg files, with an .xml file defining their properties.`,
      `That meant I could lock or unlock every page at once by changing the relevant attributes and saving the files back into the archive. This approach works regardless of the device’s speed. I was very happy when I first figured that out lol.`,
      `Back then, AI wasn’t as capable or as accessible as it is today, so I used the little Python knowledge I had and kept working on it until I could share it with my team.`,
      `As AI became more capable and easier to access, I returned to what I had learned and rebuilt the project from the very start. That eventually became this web app.`
    ]}]}
